message: >-
  If you use ENIGMA in your research, please cite this repository and the paper.
title: >-
  Executable Epistemic Contracts in Deterministic Agent Simulation:
  The ENIGMA Architecture
authors:
  - family-names: Gritsaenko
    given-names: Mikhail
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
version: 0.5.4.1.8
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22831764
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/4Um4/Enigma"
repository-code: "https://github.com/4Um4/Enigma"
abstract: >-
  In most modern LLM-based agent simulations, agent beliefs are implemented as
  prompts, and belief divergence arises as a side effect of stochastic text
  generation rather than as a designed property. We present ENIGMA, a
  deterministic multi-agent architecture in which belief divergence is a
  first-class, causally efficacious, and executably verifiable property.
  The methodological contribution is executable epistemic contracts (SUPERBOX):
  scenarios that turn epistemic claims about the system into binary,
  reproducible verdicts. The work is positioned as a systems contribution and
  a runnable reference implementation, not as a new psychological theory.
keywords:
  - deterministic agent simulation
  - epistemics
  - belief revision
  - executable contracts
  - provenance
  - LLM agents
  - Theory of Mind